msgid "Manage files across runs {#manage-files-across-runs}"
msgstr "ניהול קבצים בין הרצות {#manage-files-across-runs}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* <Admonition type=\"caution\" title=\"Placeholder content\">\n"
"- **File storage path.** `/function_user_data` is the path where the Fleets runner mounts file storage. Confirm that it is a supported path before publishing.\n"
"- **Supported file types.** The list of accepted and rejected types comes from the upload check in the gateway. Confirm the list, and whether CSV files will be accepted, before publishing.\n"
"- **Maximum file size.** Confirm the maximum file size (possibly 50 MB) before publishing.\n"
"</Admonition> */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow job works like a batch job on an HPC compute node. The job's local disk is scratch space. The job can write to it, but the workflow deletes it when the job ends. To keep files after the job ends, save them to file storage, which works like your own storage bucket. Files that you upload, and files that your workflow saves, remain in file storage, and later runs of the workflow can read them.\n"
msgstr "משימה בתהליך עבודה מנוהל פועלת כמו משימת batch על צומת חישוב של HPC. הדיסק המקומי של המשימה הוא שטח זמני. המשימה יכולה לכתוב אליו, אבל תהליך העבודה מוחק אותו כשהמשימה מסתיימת. כדי לשמור קבצים אחרי שהמשימה מסתיימת, שמרו אותם באחסון הקבצים, שפועל כמו דלי אחסון משלכם. קבצים שהעליתם, וקבצים שתהליך העבודה שלכם שומר, נשארים באחסון הקבצים, והרצות מאוחרות יותר של תהליך העבודה יכולות לקרוא אותם.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each workflow has its own file storage for each user. Other users who run the same workflow do not see your files.\n"
msgstr "לכל תהליך עבודה יש אחסון קבצים משלו לכל משתמש. משתמשים אחרים שמריצים את אותו תהליך עבודה לא רואים את הקבצים שלכם.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![File storage for the workflow sits at the center. Your local notebook reaches it with the client file methods file_upload(), files(), file_download(), and file_delete(). File storage is yours only, because other users of the workflow do not see your files. It is kept after each job ends and is shared by all of your runs, and a file with the same name replaces the earlier file. Each job sees file storage as the folder /function_user_data. Run 1 also has a local disk at /tmp, which is deleted when the job ends, and copies finished files from /tmp to /function_user_data. Run 2 reads the files that earlier runs saved.](/docs/images/managed-workflows/manage-files.svg)\n"
msgstr "![File storage for the workflow sits at the center. Your local notebook reaches it with the client file methods file_upload(), files(), file_download(), and file_delete(). File storage is yours only, because other users of the workflow do not see your files. It is kept after each job ends and is shared by all of your runs, and a file with the same name replaces the earlier file. Each job sees file storage as the folder /function_user_data. Run 1 also has a local disk at /tmp, which is deleted when the job ends, and copies finished files from /tmp to /function_user_data. Run 2 reads the files that earlier runs saved.](/docs/images/managed-workflows/manage-files.svg)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
